def govern_creative(asset, approved_kb, risk_policy):
    # 1. Invert the pipeline: restrict generation to a closed claim-graph rather than checking free text post-hoc
    claims = extract_semantic_assertions(asset)
    if not all(is_entailed_by(claim, approved_kb.evidence) for claim in claims):
        return route_to_legal(asset, reason="Unsubstantiated assertion")

    # 2. Never trust an LLM to evaluate regulatory edge cases; use strict AST/regex for black-letter prohibitions
    if contains_regulated_triggers(asset.copy, risk_policy.statutory_rules):
        return reject(asset, reason="Direct compliance violation")

    # 3. Model brand fit as outlier detection against historically approved distributions, not generative critique
    semantic_drift = compute_distribution_divergence(asset.embedding, approved_kb.brand_manifold)

    # 4. Ad networks strip C2PA; treat metadata as useless and burn disclosure directly into rendered pixels/audio
    asset = bake_visible_provenance(asset, risk_policy.jurisdiction_disclosure_rules)

    # 5. Route only the uncertain boundary layer to scarce human reviewers, sampling for drift validation
    if semantic_drift > risk_policy.human_review_threshold:
        return route_to_human(asset, priority=semantic_drift)
    return publish(asset)

Bind claims at the source;
models arrange, not assert —
audit the well once.

First cradle each claim with approved proof in sight;
If source, scope, or rights fail, it won’t take flight.

Don’t trust one grand checker to say all is well;
Use rules, risk tiers, and reviewers where meanings dwell.

Keep rights and disclosures attached as ads flow;
Bake labels in creative where metadata may go.

Shadow-test every gate, sample misses below;
We’ll narrow the danger, but still will not know.
